        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(text): strip MiniMax marker from channel replies",
        "body": "Closes #105113\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where MiniMax replies could expose the `[e~[` message-end marker in channel messages, making otherwise valid responses appear corrupted.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nThe shared model-special-token sanitizer now recognizes only this exact MiniMax control token. It keeps the existing code-region protection intact, so inline and fenced examples of the marker remain visible, while ordinary bracket text is unchanged.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers receive clean MiniMax replies through Telegram and every other delivery path that uses the shared assistant-visible-text sanitizer.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/shared/text/assistant-visible-text.test.ts` (114 tests passed)\r\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-utils.strip-model-special-tokens.test.ts` (5 tests passed)\r\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/telegram-outbound.test.ts` (15 tests passed)\r\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/shared/text/model-special-tokens.ts src/shared/text/assistant-visible-text.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-utils.strip-model-special-tokens.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/telegram-outbound.test.ts`\r\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` (clean; no accepted/actionable findings)\r\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox is unavailable in this environment because it is not authenticated to the `openclaw` organization. The focused tests above are an explicitly reported local fallback; remote build and GitHub CI remain pending.\r\n\r\nTested commit: `d140ff501333a0864d406cba7f289fdec76d228a`  \r\nRuntime model: `minimax/MiniMax-M3`\r\n\r\nI sent a Telegram message requesting a `read` of the workspace `package.json`. The final reply was delivered normally and does not contain the trailing MiniMax `[e~[` marker.\r\n\r\n*Redacted Telegram screenshot:*\r\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"2816\" alt=\"eecbf28a4ab4e0ec877600e6973792e9_720\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8e1a01d4-ac98-4ea4-9fff-39babec81b3c\" />\r\n\r\n",
